# NTP Integration Notes

## How NTP Works on ESP32
- configTime() sets up SNTP client
- getLocalTime() blocks until sync or timeout
- Returns false if sync fails within timeout

## Timezone Configuration
- IST = UTC + 5 hours 30 minutes
- GMT_OFFSET_SEC = 5 * 3600 + 30 * 60 = 19800
- DAYLIGHT_OFFSET_SEC = 0 (India has no DST)

## When NTP is Blocked (Firewall)
- getLocalTime() returns false after timeout
- isoTimestamp() returns "1970-01-01T00:00:00Z"
- Retry policy: call syncTime() again after 
  reconnection
- Alternative servers: time.nist.gov, 
  time.google.com

## ISO-8601 Format
- Format: YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS
- Example: 2026-06-06T19:30:00
- Used in JSON payloads for cloud dashboard
